/**
 * MM105: Medi's knowledge base, generated from the site's own registries.
 *
 * Pure: `buildMediKnowledge()` returns `{ "<relative path>": "<file body>" }`;
 * `scripts/export-medi.ts` (`npm run export:medi`) writes it to
 * `../media_manipulator_api/internal/assistant/knowledge/`, where the API embeds
 * it (`go:embed`) and ranks it with BM25 (design §7.1, ticket decisions 1–3).
 * Winny's pattern (winapps_next `lib/winny-export.ts`): generated, never
 * hand-edited, regenerated by one script; plus every editor's capabilities, so
 * Medi learns a new effect the day it ships.
 *
 * Doc shape (every .md): the generated line, `# Title`, bullets Route / Kind /
 * Category / Slug, then `## Summary`, `## Details`, `## Search keywords`,
 * `## Links`, `## Opens`. The Go loader (`internal/assistant/corpus.go`) reads
 * exactly these headings.
 *
 * Tier numbers never appear (decision 3): the API injects the live
 * `/api/tiers` numbers at request time. Sentences that state a plan's daily
 * count, a price or a per-plan size cap are dropped from the exported copy
 * (`stripTierNumbers`), and `knowledgeExport.test.ts` fails if any slips through.
 */
